Dear Sir or Madam,

The Bundesnetzagentur, acting as the German market surveillance
authority for AI systems, is investigating the creation and
dissemination of two photorealistic deepfake videos of a German
mayoral candidate (case no. KI-MUE-2026/0233). The videos were
generated with your model "Nordlys Vision 3" through the downstream
service "SzenenWerk Studio" operated by Kampagnenschmiede GmbH,
Berlin. According to the evidence before us, the C2PA provenance
signature and the visible watermark embedded by your model were
removed at export stage, and the videos were published without any
marking.

In coordination with the competent Danish authority (in copy), and
with reference to the cooperation obligations of providers of
general-purpose AI models under Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, we
kindly ask you to provide, by 6 July 2026:

1. The generation logs of the API jobs NLV3-88412, NLV3-88467,
NLV3-88529 and NLV3-88603 (26 May to 1 June 2026), including any
policy notices issued to the integrator or end user.

2. A copy of your integrator agreement (tier "Studio") with
Kampagnenschmiede GmbH, in particular the clauses implementing
section 3.2 of your Acceptable Use Policy (removal of markings only
against equivalent substitute marking), and a description of how
compliance with these clauses is monitored and enforced in
practice.

3. Information on whether your systems detected the removal of the
provenance marking in this case, and on any measures taken against
the integrator since.

4. The current version of your training-content summary and
copyright policy published under Article 53 of Regulation (EU)
2024/1689, together with information on the data sources relevant
to photorealistic renditions of real persons. Please note that the
exact scope of the applicable provisions is subject to official
verification in view of pending EU omnibus amendments.

Please quote our case number in all correspondence. This request is
addressed to you as a voluntary cooperation request; we reserve
formal measures through the competent authorities.

Yours faithfully,

